/* ================================================================
   TYPOGRAPHY AUDIT — ELITE BASELINE CORRECTION
   
   Problem inventory from audit:
   
   CRITICAL (sub-11px — illegible on standard monitors):
   — .52rem (8.3px): sidebar-dept-sub, user-role, pd-stat-l
   — .55rem (8.8px): sidebar-section-title, pd-date-k, sm-preview-role
   — 8px: avatar initials, timeline cell labels, stage nodes
   — 9px: 88 instances across badges, labels, meta — the most widespread issue
   
   SIGNIFICANT (borderline):
   — .6rem (9.6px): nm-type-badge, pd-schedule-label
   — .65rem (10.4px): profile shift times, research meta
   — 10px: used for labels that need 11px minimum
   
   FONT FAMILY:
   — Fraunces referenced in 3 places where Instrument Serif is the
     declared display face — inconsistency in the display serif
   — DM Mono used in 276 places, often at tiny sizes where
     monospace + small = doubly illegible
   
   LETTER-SPACING:
   — 31 instances of .1em+ tracking — correctly reserved for
     uppercase labels. But when combined with 9px type it
     makes text unreadable at distance.
   
   STANDARD APPLIED:
   Elite medical platforms (Epic MyChart, Veeva Vault, REDCap Pro,
   Medidata Rave) and elite SaaS (Linear, Notion, Figma) share:
   — Body: 14px minimum, typically 14-15px
   — Secondary/meta: 12px minimum
   — Labels/caps: 11px with tracking (absolute floor)
   — Initials in avatars: 9-10px is acceptable ONLY in 28px+ containers
   — Sidebar nav: 13px minimum
   — Section group labels: 10-11px with tracking
   
   STRATEGY:
   Rather than hunting 200+ individual rules, we override by
   ROLE — every class that serves a given typographic function
   gets corrected in one place. !important required throughout
   to beat both style.css base rules and #app-scoped inline rules.
================================================================ */


/* ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   1. SIDEBAR TYPOGRAPHY — complete correction
   Body root is 15px, so rem values below resolve as noted.
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

/* Sidebar nav link text: was .825rem (~12.4px) — too small for nav */
.sidebar-menu-link {
  font-size: 13px !important;  /* crisp, scan-friendly */
}

/* Sidebar section titles: was .55rem (8.3px) — genuinely illegible */
.sidebar-section-title {
