/* ================================================================
   §19-21  RESEARCH HUB — COMPREHENSIVE UI FIX
   
   Issues from screenshots:
   
   STUDIES LIST (Image 1):
   1. Phase badges: red/pink/yellow palette reads as urgency not phase
      → Softer, more academic colour palette
   2. rht-title truncates with ellipsis unnecessarily → allow wrap
   3. rht-protocol: 9px → 11px
   4. Row hover: rgba(.025) invisible → proper hover
   5. Right chevron: more visible
   6. rht-row padding: too tight → more breathing room
   
   LINE DETAIL (Image 2):
   7. L6 number in pink (#9d174d) reads as alert → use clinical blue
      for the large display number, keep accent colour for the stripe
   8. Description text only uses half width → fix layout
   9. Health strip: all warning counts same visual weight as active
      → differentiate with colour semantics
   10. rhub-ltab active: dark underline → teal
   11. Study rows in detail: more structure, readable
   12. Empty space right of study cards → fix grid
   13. ⚠ incompleto badge: too much padding → tighter
   14. rfc-head labels: too faint
   15. rfc-val: proper size
   
   PATTERN (throughout):
   16. Phase badge on inline list: 28px too small → 36px
   17. Phase badge in detail hero: 44px inline style → ensure consistent
   18. Completeness missing field tags → clearer
================================================================ */


/* ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   1. PHASE BADGES — academic palette, not urgency
   
   Roman numerals in clinical trials are stage markers, not alerts.
   Current palette: red (IV), blue (I), green (II), yellow (III).
   Red for Phase IV (the most common, mature phase) is backwards.
   
   New palette: neutral-to-warm academic spectrum.
   Phase I  → blue (exploratory, early)
   Phase II → teal (intermediate)
   Phase III → indigo (advanced, pivotal)
   Phase IV → slate-blue (post-market, established)
   Non-phase (Observational etc) → warm grey
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

/* List view badge: 36px */
#app .rht-phase-badge {
  width: 36px !important;
  height: 36px !important;
  border-radius: 9px !important;
  font-size: 12px !important;
  font-weight: 700 !important;
  letter-spacing: -.01em !important;
  flex-shrink: 0 !important;
  color: #fff !important;
  display: flex !important;
  align-items: center !important;
  justify-content: center !important;
  box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,.12) !important;
}

/* Phase colours: academic spectrum */
#app .rht-phase--pI    { background: #2563eb !important; }  /* blue — exploratory */
#app .rht-phase--pII   { background: #059669 !important; color: #fff !important; }  /* emerald */
#app .rht-phase--pIII  { background: #7c3aed !important; }  /* indigo — pivotal */
#app .rht-phase--pIV   { background: #1a4f8a !important; }  /* clinical blue — established */

/* Detail hero badge: 44px inline override */
#app .rhub-study-hero .rht-phase-badge,
#app [style*="width:44px"] .rht-phase-badge,
#app .rht-phase-badge[style*="44px"] {
  width: 44px !important;
  height: 44px !important;
