/* ================================================================
   §29  L-NUMBER TYPOGRAPHY + FORM SPECIFICITY FIXES
   
   L-numbers: replace heavy italic serif identity with a light,
   embedded clinical label. The number should be secondary to
   the line title, not the visual anchor of the card.
   
   Forms: beat the HTML line-745 override using html #app prefix.
   All inputs get visible 1.5px borders in clinical blue system.
================================================================ */


/* ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   L-NUMBER REDESIGN
   
   Current: Instrument Serif italic 44px in line accent colour
   Problem: Too dominant, decorative, heavy. Reads as magazine
            logo, not a clinical line identifier.
   
   Solution: DM Mono 13px light, subdued grey/blue, embedded
             as a small label in the top-left corner. The line
             TITLE becomes the primary identifier.
   
   Before: huge italic "L1" competing with the title
   After:  small "L1" label, title leads, stats support
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

