/* ================================================================
   §44  PUBLICATIONS + NEWS DRAWER — READING EXPERIENCE ELITE
        + 30 MODULE IMPROVEMENTS
   
   The drawer opens from the right as a slide panel.
   Question: is this the best? Answer: YES for clinical use —
   it keeps list context visible (you can see prev/next).
   But the reading EXPERIENCE needs major improvements:
   
   Current problems in the reading experience:
   - nrd-body padding 2rem 2.5rem: good but no max-width centering
   - nrd-title has no space above it (eyebrow runs into it)
   - Prev/Next nav is all inline styles — fragile and ugly
   - nrd-status-pill font-size: 9px — violation
   - nrd-vis-pill font-size: 9px — violation
   - Photo story: images have no consistent sizing
   - Publication type: journal/authors/DOI not fully styled
   - The 780px drawer at 1080p = 72% of screen — acceptable
   - No reading-mode distinction: article vs update look similar
   - nrd-photo-caption: uses 0.9375rem — needs explicit value
   - Missing: article "hero" first paragraph treatment
   - Missing: inline images in article body
   - Missing: pull-quote treatment
   - Footer buttons: "Back" = left arrow; "Archive" = bin; both need icons
   - Word count bar: too small and hard to read
   
   LIST VIEW improvements:
   - news-card height inconsistent between types
   - Highlight cards should show a cover image thumbnail
   - The STATUS panel (right sidebar collapse) is styled poorly
================================================================ */


