   ROOT CAUSE of "hover around to detect click":
   Many interactive elements have padding:0 in the HTML block.
   With padding:0, the click area = content box only (the text/icon).
   The visual size comes from min-height or child dimensions,
   but the POINTER HIT TEST uses the element's own padding box.
   
   Result: you see a 40px button but can only click a 16px strip
   (the text height), so you need to hover right over the text.
   
