/* ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   §61  TAB-BAR OVERFLOW GUARD — universal anti-overlap
   Root cause (verified via layout testing): horizontal tab bars are
   flex containers whose tab items default to flex-shrink:1, so when
   the bar is narrower than the sum of its tabs the items collapse
   below their content width and the labels overlap. Fix: tab items
   never shrink; the bar scrolls horizontally instead of overlapping.
   Both declarations are non-destructive — flex-shrink:0 cannot break
   a bar that already fits, and overflow-x:auto only engages on real
   overflow. Scoped to genuine tab/subtab bars only.
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
#app .nm-tabs,
#app .oco-tabs,
#app .rhub-line-tabs,
#app .sm-edit-tabs,
#app .oce-type-tabs,
#app .rha-subtabs,
